        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS take great pleasure in introducing this substantial four-bedroom semi-detached property with a long list of additional benefits to the market in the ever-popular Cappaghmore Estate, Dublin 22. This impressive property offers 4 bedrooms, a self-contained unit to the side, a part converted attic and also a large unit to the rear offering versatility for a variety of uses. Cappaghmore is a highly sought-after residential location, surrounded by an excellent range of amenities including well-regarded primary and secondary schools, recreational and leisure facilities, The Mill Shopping Centre and a selection of bars, cafés and restaurants. The area is exceptionally well serviced by public transport, with direct bus routes providing easy access to Dublin City Centre, while the M50 motorway and Red Cow Luas Stop are also within convenient reach. Ideally positioned within easy reach of Clondalkin Village, In brief, this property consists of; Entrance hall, open plan lounge/diner, kitchen breakfast room and access into the converted garage which currently offers a self-contained one bedroom unit with bedroom/living area, kitchen, wc and shower to the ground floor. Upstairs you will find 4 well proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. Externally to the rear is arguably one of this property's major selling points. You will find a larger than average sunny rear garden with large patio area, lawn area and a sectioned off portion which offers access to the garden unit which provides endless scope for either an office, a sperate self-contained studio or garden room. Not only does the front offer an abundance of curb appeal, you will also find a large driveway for off road parking.  No 68 come to the market in good condition throughout but the opportunity on offer makes this property stand out. With extended accommodation, future scope and excellent location, interest is sure to be seen from a long list of buyers and based on recent success specifically in this development we know this will be extremely popular so please contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers to register your interest and to arrange a viewing.\n\nFeatures\nBer D1\nc. 135 Sqm\nExtended to rear\nSelf-contained unit to side\nXL garden room with endless scope\nLarge driveway to front\nPart converted attic\n4/5 bedrooms\n2 Bath\nSought after location\nClose to amenities\nMature location\nFantastic opportunity\nDouble glazed windows\nCall today to arrange a viewing!\n\n\nDirections\nHeading out of Clondalkin village, head towards the Ninth Lock. Go over the bridge and just after the traffic light junction of at Station Road. Roughly 100m on your left hand side you will find the entrance to the Cappaghmore development. .\n"
      },
